%% DM26-0670

%% A client gives up a topic, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md "The flows"). The broker does this by
%% itself too, when authority no longer allows a subscription (broker/client_subscription).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (facade and transport)
    participant Listener
    participant Session as SessionAgent
    participant Broker
    participant Topics as TopicManager
    participant Subs as SubscriberManager
    participant Sub as SubscriberAgent
    participant SM as SessionManager

    Client->>Client: the facade forgets any standing refusal of the topic
    Client->>Listener: UnsubscribeRequest(registration_id, topic)
    Listener->>Session: UnsubscribeRequest(topic)
    Session->>Broker: UnsubscribeRequest(registration_id, topic)
    par side by side, neither waits for the other
        Broker->>Topics: UnsubscribeRequest
        Note over Topics: The TopicManager has no arm for it, and logs it as unexpected.
    and
        Broker->>Subs: UnsubscribeRequest
        Subs->>Sub: stop, and what it held goes with it
        Sub->>Topics: TopicHold(not holding), if it was holding the topic back
        Subs->>SM: UnsubscribeAcknowledgment(registration_id, topic, Ok)
        SM->>Session: UnsubscribeAcknowledgment
        Session->>Listener: UnsubscribeAcknowledgment
        Listener-->>Client: UnsubscribeAcknowledgment(topic, Ok)
    end
    Note over Topics,Sub: So the topic keeps the dead reference until its next publish finds it has ended, and drops it then.
